{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>All the days.</b> Meaning: as long as his plague — which is his sin — remains upon him, so too does he remain in the impurity of his tzara'at. And the verse's saying <b>he shall be impure</b> means he shall remain in his impurity. And the verse's saying <b>he is impure</b> — this is along the lines of the verse (Jeremiah 2:19) ״תְּיַסְּרֵךְ רָעָתֵךְ״, for HaShem blessed be He does not make him impure; rather, he is impure of himself, on account of his own deeds, and HaShem does nothing to him. And so it says (Lamentations 3:39) ״מַה יִּתְאוֹנֵן אָדָם חַי גֶּבֶר עַל חֲטָאָיו״, and they of blessed memory expounded it (Yalkut Shimoni 2220) — see their words there. And see what I have written (Genesis 4:7) on the verse ״הֲלֹא אִם תֵּיטִיב שְׂאֵת״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:56:08.908550780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}